Here, we constructed a random Gaussian matrix of size 50x50 with mean zero and standard deviation one. We calculated the eigenvalues of this matrix, and plotted a histogram of the logarithm of the eigenvalues. The expectation is that the eigenvalue distribution should follow a semi-circle shape in the complex logarithmic space, which means that most eigenvalues should fall within unit circle and there should be few outliers that lie far from the unit circle.This is because the eigenvectors of a Gaussian matrix follow the multivariate Normal distribution.
